  "summary": "A Mini Pupper sized robot dog: twelve MG90S metal-gear servos (hip, thigh and knee per leg) on a PCA9685, an ESP32 runs the trot gait with an MPU-6050 for balance and an HC-SR04 in the head, on two 18650 cells.",
  "spec": {
    "name": "12-Servo Quadruped Robot Dog",
    "function": "A four-legged walking robot with three joints per leg: twelve MG90S servos on a PCA9685 driver, an ESP32 runs the trot gait and balances with an MPU-6050, an HC-SR04 in the head sees obstacles, and two 18650 cells feed a 6 V servo rail through a 5 A step-down.",
    "quote": "Next one is a robot dog, Mini Pupper size: twelve servos, three per leg, so it can trot and lean. MG90S metal gear, a PCA9685 for the servos, an ESP32 with an IMU, and an ultrasonic sensor in the head. Two 18650 cells. In a trot two legs carry the whole dog, so the knee servos need twice the torque that takes. It must not fall over when someone bumps it, at least 20 degrees, run an hour of walking, stay under 800 grams and under 120 euros.",
